WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Let’s talk about the 
fighting in Ethiopia.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.480
The government’s launched
 a military offensive 

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.800
in the north in a region 
called Tigray.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.360
At the centre of it all is Ethiopia’s prime minister 

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.680
a Nobel Peace Prize winner.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.000
He would know. 

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.240
Abiy used to be a soldier  

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.800
who now has another 
fight on his hands.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.880
So how did the fighting start?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.800
And what is this conflict 
really about?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.360
Ethiopia is a huge country

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.000
with many ethnic groups and political parties. 

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.520
Governing them has
 at times been difficult

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.040
for the central government 
in Addis Ababa.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.200
There have been a few 
years of economic growth 

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.720
and relative calm. 

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.040
Now, though, things are starting to heat up. 

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.920
Here’s why. 

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.960
Ethiopia is divided
into 10 regions.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.360
They loosely represent different ethnic groups.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.160
Each one has some autonomy

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.360
but the centre of power is in Ethiopia’s capital.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.560
Tigray, where most of the fighting has been happening

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.680
is in the north. 

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.840
The government there is called the TPLF.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.920
And it even has its own regional army.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.560
The TPLF wasn’t just in charge of the Tigray region.  

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.800
It pretty much ran the country for nearly 30 years

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.720
even though the Tigrayans are a minority

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.080
just 6% of the population.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.600
The TPLF was the head of a coalition of regional parties.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.000
But many people saw it as autocratic and dysfunctional. 

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.880
They locked up 
hundreds of journalists 

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.960
and political dissidents.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.120
Massive protests eventually brought them down.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.840
The chaos allowed Abiy Ahmed, a young leader

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.360
seen as a visionary, 
to get elected.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.520
He’s from the Oromo

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.480
Ethiopia’s largest 
ethnic group.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.880
Abiy even won a Nobel Prize for making peace

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.280
with Eritrea next door.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.440
For as long as the TPLF 
was in power

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.160
Ethiopia was involved in a border standoff with Eritrea.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.440
So they didn’t appreciate Abiy’s new friendship

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.920
with the Eritrean president.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.040
So here’s Prime Minister Abiy with a Nobel Prize

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.000
and all these ambitious ideas about how to keep the peace 

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.920
in Ethiopia and modernise 
the economy.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.280
Part of his plan was to disband the old governing coalition 

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.880
and unify the country under
 a new Prosperity Party.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.240
But some, including the TPLF, saw that as taking power

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.720
from the regions. 

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.600
They also saw it as a 
power grab by Abiy.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.760
The TPLF pulled 
out completely.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.680
And they’re accused of doing all kinds of things

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.960
to sabotage Abiy’s success.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.360
Abiy Ahmed removed members of the TPLF

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.640
from top positions.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.080
Many were arrested and prosecuted for corruption 

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.200
and abuse of power.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:28.040
So Abiy Ahmed, who at 44 is Africa’s youngest leader

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.880
made a lot of enemies
 really quick.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.600
Two years ago someone even tried to assassinate him.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.000
So that brings us to what’s happening now.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.600
Back in March Abiy’s government 

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.200
postponed elections because of the pandemic.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.400
But in September the TPLF held one anyway.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.000
That escalated things. 

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.640
The parliament called 
the vote illegal. 

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.880
The TPLF said it didn’t recognise Abiy 

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.280
as a legitimate leader. 

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.760
And TPLF forces attacked a government military base.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.920
So Abiy sent in troops and it all blew up from there.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.720
Now this is where we’d show you footage of the war 

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.560
but we just don’t have much. 

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.520
The government has 
cut Tigray off

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.880
the roads, the airport 
and the internet.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.600
So here’s what we’re hearing.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.760
We know the government is launching air strikes.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.360
The TPLF has launched rocket attacks of its own

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.240
even across Tigray’s borders.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.560
Soldiers on both sides 
are being killed.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.880
Civilians too. 

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.880
We’re just not sure how many.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.440
Thousands of people 
have been forced 

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.840
to leave their homes.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.840
Many are crossing into Sudan.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.200
And we’re already hearing reports of terrible violence

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.600
though we can’t independently verify them.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.240
Amnesty International is investigating potential 

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.520
war crimes including hundreds of people 

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.280
reportedly hacked to death.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.160
The other worry is that 
this war could

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.600
spread and drag in 
other countries.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.520
And it’s kind of 
already happening.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.800
The TPLF says its old enemy Eritrea has sent troops 

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.800
to help Ethiopian government forces — which Eritrea denies.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.400
Whatever’s happening the point is the TPLF sees Eritrea

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.040
and Abiy Ahmed as being 
on the same side.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.520
Which could explain why 
the TPLF has now 

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.440
turned on its neighbour.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.760
So what do Ethiopians think of what’s going on?

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.800
Some support the 
offensive on Tigray. 

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.840
These people for instance
are donating blood

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.440
for wounded soldiers.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.880
Abiy’s supporters feel he had no choice but to act

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.920
because they say the TPLF undermined him at every turn

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.960
and stirred up ethnic violence.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.080
But other Ethiopians say 
the prime minister

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.080
isn’t living up to his promises.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.200
And that instead of pursuing peace he’s chosen war. 

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.200
In a lot of ways this 
is a battle between  

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.880
the old guard and the new.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.160
The TPLF started this fight 

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.640
but now it’s about 
how it’s going to end.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.560
Whatever Abiy did to earn 
his Nobel Peace Prize

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.160
he’ll be feeling the pressure 
to do it again.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.920
This story is moving fast

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.400
and there's a lot happening in Ethiopia, not just in Tigray.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.280
We have a lot of reporters
in the region

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.320
covering the story so make sure to visit aljazeera.com

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:50.960
to get the very latest. 

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:51.800
We’ll see you next week. 

